{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3257","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3257","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3257\",\"parent_revision\":\"0270bf60a3fa9e0b52c61800aefb61af84ca38830d1ba55ffc31ad91a8fbb7dc\",\"root_revision\":\"0270bf60a3fa9e0b52c61800aefb61af84ca38830d1ba55ffc31ad91a8fbb7dc\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-27\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nLanguage manifests (e.g. plugins/python3-development/manifests/python3/language-manifest.yaml, manifests/python3-cli/language-manifest.yaml) declare a `stage_skills` map (discovery, design, planning-context-integration, planning-task-decomposition, implementation, testing-forensic-review, testing-final-verification \u2192 lists of name strings). Two different code paths consume this same map with incompatible expectations for what the names mean:\\n\\n1. `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md`'s Phase 3 resolves the `design` entry specifically via `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__profile_load(agent_name='{value}')` \u2014 expects an agent name (bare or plugin-qualified), resolved against `plugins/*/agents/**/*.md`.\\n\\n2. `plugins/development-harness/scripts/dispatch_helper.py` (line 94: `domain_skills = manifest.stage_skills.get(stage, [])`, line 60: formats each as `` `Skill(skill=\\\"{skill}\\\")` ``) treats every `stage_skills` entry for every stage \u2014 design included \u2014 as a skill name, resolved against `plugins/*/skills/*/SKILL.md`.\\n\\nNo single value in `stage_skills.design` (or any other stage) can satisfy both consumers, since agent names and skill names are drawn from disjoint namespaces (confirmed: `python-cli-design-spec` exists only under `plugins/python3-development/agents/`, not `skills/`).\\n\\nVerified via git history and current directory listing: this is not a new problem introduced by PR #3256 \u2014 no skill named `python3-design` (the pre-existing, also-broken value) ever existed in this repo either, so the `dispatch_helper.py` consumer was already non-functional for this field before PR #3256 and remains non-functional after it. PR #3256 only fixes the `profile_load`/agent-name consumer (verified working) \u2014 it does not, and could not without a design decision, also fix `dispatch_helper.py`'s skill-name consumer.\\n\\n**Not yet investigated**: whether `dispatch_helper.py`'s generic-stage-agent dispatch path is actually invoked in current production usage for Python projects, or whether it is legacy/dormant code \u2014 this materially affects urgency and the right fix (separate field per consumer vs. deprecating one consumer vs. unifying resolution).\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Surfaced by a Codex review comment on PR #3256; verified directly against both consumers' source\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-27\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"204e6a32c604e4c1bfd46fbb5c04d6b55c2eda8099ea59cf9e8fdf2de77fc8ca\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRBaqxQ\"}"}